    <item>
      <title>Travel and Accomodations</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/2026/travel/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/2026/travel/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;travel-details&#34;&gt;Travel Details&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The best way to get to Santa Barbara is to fly to Santa Barbara Municipal Airport (SBA), which is 7 miles from downtown Santa Barbara where the conference will be hosted. This airport is regional, so unless you are in the western United States you will likely need to transfer. The other option would be to fly to Los Angeles International Airport (LAX), and then rent a car or take a shuttle like the &lt;a style=&#34;color: #024acfff&#34; href=&#34;https://www.sbairbus.com&#34;&gt;SB Airbus.&lt;/a&gt; This second option may be cheaper but will require a few hours of driving.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
